End the Claude status adapter's ancestor walk at any ngterm origin. The walk stopped at `ngterm` only, so in a session of a headless origin (`ngterm-headless`), or past the session server that holds a live session's shell (`ngterm-session`), it went on into whatever started the origin: an origin started from a coding agent's shell made every pane's agent a silent worker. Both forms. Applied after 0009-claude-background-job.patch.

diff --git a/ngterm-claude-status.ps1 b/ngterm-claude-status.ps1
index b240357..cccd891 100644
--- a/ngterm-claude-status.ps1
+++ b/ngterm-claude-status.ps1
@@ -117,7 +117,9 @@ function Test-Worker {
       $previous = ''
     }
     if ($agents -gt 1) { return $true } # a second agent above mine: I am a worker, not the pane's agent
-    if (@('login', 'ngterm') -contains $base) { break } # reached the pane boundary
+    # the pane boundary: the app, a headless origin, or the session server that holds a live session's shell.
+    # Whatever is above started the origin and is not in the pane.
+    if (@('login', 'ngterm', 'ngterm-headless', 'ngterm-session') -contains $base) { break }
     $child = $process
   }
   return $false
diff --git a/ngterm-claude-status.sh b/ngterm-claude-status.sh
index 5eaf048..16d1152 100755
--- a/ngterm-claude-status.sh
+++ b/ngterm-claude-status.sh
@@ -88,7 +88,9 @@ for _ in 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8; do
     prev_agent=
   fi
   [ "$agents" -gt 1 ] && exit 0        # a second agent above mine: I am a worker, not the pane's agent
-  case "$base" in login | ngterm) break ;; esac # reached the pane boundary
+  # the pane boundary: the app, a headless origin, or the session server that holds a live session's shell. Whatever
+  # is above started the origin (an agent's shell that ran ngterm-headless, say) and is not in the pane.
+  case "$base" in login | ngterm | ngterm-headless | ngterm-session) break ;; esac
   p=$ppid
 done
 
